    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1415">

                <pb facs="1128" n="1012" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1012"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/1749.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your January 4. You will repeat it to the American Legations in Costa Rica, San
                    Salvador and Guatemala, adding that the Department requests a full report after
                    careful investigation. Request of Heimke<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1415-f1"/>
                    transmission of copies of intercepted correspondence mentioned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1415-f1" n="3" xml:id="d1415-f1-content">
                <p>American Minister to Salvador.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
